35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, the data is eye-opening! It turns out most of our costs are fixed, like hall hire and insurance. We have to cover those regardless of attendance, so we really need a predictable income stream.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It is interesting that costs are fixed, but we must be careful. I noticed that when we introduced door charges for outings, weekday attendance dropped significantly and never recovered. People seem to hesitate more now.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Takumi,,It's not just about the money. I found that the same nine people are doing all the setup and locking up. It's totally unfair that a few people carry the whole club while others just show up.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The administrative burden is far higher than I suspected. Chasing small, individual payments takes six times longer than a yearly collection. We cannot afford a system that creates this much unpaid labor for the treasurer.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,I found something really important! A lot of people who came to taster evenings didn't join because they didn't want to pay for a whole year at once. Even mid-year joiners needed special calculations to feel okay joining.,"{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, @Kenji, I see the problem. We need a stable way to cover those fixed costs, but chasing people is a nightmare and scary for newcomers. How can we make it predictable without being too rigid?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, I believe we should avoid any system that requires members to pay per visit. If people have to weigh the cost every time they consider coming, they may simply stop attending.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, I get that, but we can't just ignore the imbalance. If the same few people are doing all the work and paying the same as ghosts, it's just wrong. We need a way to reward the regulars.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, rewarding regulars is a fair goal, but not if it complicates the bookkeeping. If we implement a complex tiered system, we risk burning out the next treasurer with endless calculations and chasing small sums.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, I understand the treasurer's work is hard, but if we make it too strict, we'll lose new friends! We need a way to let people drift in without feeling pressured by a huge bill.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Kenji, @Toshio, what if we have a base fee for the fixed costs and then something simpler for the rest? We can't keep guessing, but we can't make the treasurer's life a nightmare either!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, a base fee is a gentle solution. As long as it is a one-time payment, it removes the psychological barrier of a per-visit cost, allowing members to feel they truly belong without hesitation.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Mio, a base fee is fine, but it doesn't fix the unfairness. If we just have one fee, the people doing all the work still get the short end of the stick. We need a real incentive for the regulars.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, incentives are useless if the system collapses because no one wants to be treasurer. Any ""reward"" that requires tracking individual attendance or hours will only increase the administrative burden we must avoid. Simple is sustainable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I get that it feels unfair, but if we make it too complicated, it might feel like a club for ""insiders"" only. Let's find a way to be fair that doesn't scare people away!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, @Takumi, I hear you both! We need to cover those fixed costs reliably, but we can't kill the treasurer or alienate new members. Let's see the options and find a balance that's stable and simple!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I hope the options provide a way to maintain the club's welcoming spirit. It is vital that we prioritize a sense of belonging over a strict accounting of every visit.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm not letting this go. Belonging is great, but it shouldn't be built on the backs of nine people. If the options don't address the imbalance of work and use, they aren't fair.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, fairness is not just about who uses the club, but also about who manages it. A system that is ""fair"" to members but impossible to administer is a failure. I will vote for the simplest option.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I hope we can find a way to keep things friendly! Let's look at the options and pick one that lets everyone feel welcome, whether they're new or have been here forever!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
