60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Looking at the options, Option A is the most stable for our fixed costs. It ensures we have the money for the hall and insurance upfront without any guesswork or chasing people all year!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Mio. Option A is the most serene choice. It removes the hesitation of per-event costs, ensuring that members feel they belong without having to weigh the price of attending each evening.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A is just ignoring the problem. It's the same old system where the regulars do all the work and the ghosts get a free ride. We need something like Option B to actually recognize different levels of use.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option B still requires the treasurer to track which member belongs to which tier and manage different payment amounts. Option A is the only choice that truly minimizes the administrative burden and prevents burnout.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I see your point, but Option B feels like it creates ""ranks"" of members. That might make newcomers feel like they don't belong unless they're ""top tier."" Option A is simpler and friendlier for everyone!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Takumi, I understand you want fairness, but Option B could be a nightmare for the treasurer and might lead to more payment delays. Option A gives us the financial certainty we desperately need to keep the club running!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, while I understand your desire for fairness, we must consider the psychological cost. Option C would be the most damaging, as it forces a decision every time someone considers joining us. Option A preserves the peace.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, peace isn't the same as fairness. If we just stick with Option A, we're telling the people who actually run this club that their effort doesn't matter. Option B is a fair compromise.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, your definition of fairness ignores the treasurer. Option B creates more categories to track and more potential for errors. Option A is the only sustainable path that ensures the role remains fillable.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, @Mio, you're right about the stress! And @Takumi, I really don't want anyone feeling ignored. But Option C is too scary for new people, and Option B feels like a club for ""insiders."" Let's go with A!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Mio"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@Takumi, I really wish we could reward the regulars, but we can't risk the club's finances or the treasurer's sanity. Option A is the only way to guarantee our fixed costs are covered without any guesswork!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, I believe the greatest fairness is providing a space where everyone feels welcome to return. Option A ensures that the act of attending remains a simple joy, rather than a financial calculation.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, it's not a ""calculation"" to want a fair system. If we keep ignoring the people doing all the work, they'll eventually just stop. Option B is the only way to actually fix the imbalance.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, if the regulars stop because of a flat fee, that is a management issue, not a bookkeeping one. However, if the treasurer quits because of a complex system, the entire club stops. Option A is the only logical choice.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I really hope the regulars know we appreciate them! But I'm worried that if we make it too complicated, new people will be too scared to join. Let's keep it simple and welcoming with Option A!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,"I've listened to everyone, and while I see Takumi's point, we can't gamble with our stability. Option A is the only way to ensure our fixed costs are covered and the treasurer survives! I vote for Option A.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe the psychological ease of belonging is paramount. To avoid the hesitation that erodes our community, we must remove any financial barriers to attendance. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Takumi,,"I'm the only one fighting for the people who actually keep this place running. If we don't recognize the effort of the regulars, this club will collapse anyway. I vote for Option B.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The data is clear: chasing small sums is a drain on our resources and our people. To ensure the club's survival and the treasurer's sanity, we must prioritize simplicity. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I really want everyone to feel like they belong here, and Option A is the friendliest way to do that! Let's keep it simple so nobody feels left out. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
